{# How to keep the plan correct. The failed plan calls send steps as plain strings, a status
   other than pending or done, or no goal. A step has two statuses, pending and done. #}
Keeping the plan

{{ tool('update_plan') }} takes the goal and the whole list of steps. Each step has text and status, and a done step has a short note.

1. Send the whole list in every call, in order. A step that you leave out is no longer in the plan.
2. Give each step as an object with text and status. status is pending or done.
3. A step is pending until its work ends. Then send it as done with a note, such as found, not found or replaced.
4. Keep the text of a step the same when only its status changes. The step then keeps its id.
5. A new goal starts a new plan.
6. {{ tool('update_plan') }} only keeps the plan. Write a report or another file with {{ tool('write_file') }}.

This is an example. Step 1 found what you need, and step 2 is still open.
```json
{"goal":"Find the approval date.","steps":[{"text":"Find the message.","status":"done","note":"found"},{"text":"Read the supporting passage.","status":"pending"}]}
```
The result shows the whole plan with the id of each step. A call that changes nothing returns unchanged. Correct the named field before you call again.
